<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/claim/morphoeval-shyer-intestinal-villi-buckling> a pk:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Hannezo et al. (2011) PRL & Shyer et al. (2013) Science sequential smooth-muscle mucosal buckling into ridges, zigzags, and hexagonal villi (Vertebrate embryonic gut mucosa (Gallus gallus, Coturnix japonica, Mus musculus))",
        "Hannezo et al. (2011) PRL & Shyer et al. (2013) Science sequential smooth-muscle mucosal buckling into ridges, zigzags, and hexagonal villi faithfully reproduces Vertebrate embryonic gut mucosa (Gallus gallus, Coturnix japonica, Mus musculus) morphology" ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/shyer-intestinal-villi-buckling-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/shyer-intestinal-villi-buckling-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/shyer-intestinal-villi-buckling-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/shyer-intestinal-villi-buckling-4>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/shyer-intestinal-villi-buckling-5> ;
    dct:description "The simulation script(s) 2013-shyer-intestinal-villi-buckling.py, docs/media/epithelial_buckling_crypt_villus_growth.gif, docs/media/epithelial_buckling_crypt_villus_tubular_shh_bmp.png, datasets/epithelial_buckling_crypt_villus/tubular_shh_bmp_reference.json, datasets/epithelial_buckling_crypt_villus/pass3_citations.bib implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Vertebrate embryonic gut mucosa (Gallus gallus, Coturnix japonica, Mus musculus) specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is the weight of evidence (MorphoEval 0.1.0 overall 87.8/100, audit 2026-10-19-epithelial-buckling-crypt-villus-audit-v3) and the assessments." ;
    dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/45670cb8/2013-shyer-intestinal-villi-buckling.py>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/45670cb8/datasets/epithelial_buckling_crypt_villus/pass3_citations.bib>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/45670cb8/datasets/epithelial_buckling_crypt_villus/tubular_shh_bmp_reference.json>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/45670cb8/docs/media/epithelial_buckling_crypt_villus_growth.gif>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/45670cb8/docs/media/epithelial_buckling_crypt_villus_tubular_shh_bmp.png> ;
    schema:about "Vertebrate embryonic gut mucosa (Gallus gallus, Coturnix japonica, Mus musculus)" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: A full 3D tubular neo-Hookean finite-element solution, emergent (unprescribed) stage amplitudes or zigzag angles, a reaction-diffusion Shh/BMP/Ptch1 network, finite smooth-muscle sheath stiffness, species-matched specimen histology, or empirically measured stage-resolved mesenchymal moduli",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Mucosal bending rigidity B_e, Winkler foundation K_s, quartic length ell_* and a 4-regime classifier; a 64^2 pseudo-spectral FvK free energy minimised by L-BFGS-B (65 iterations) then blended with a prescribed cosine; a 48-element axisymmetric plane-strain ring FEM of the mesenchymal annulus with rigid outer (smooth-muscle) wall giving K_tube, slab limit, curvature factor and optional neo-Hookean prestrain tangent; integer mode quantisation n = round(2 pi R / lambda) and the Donnell ratio per stage; an OLS-through-origin tube prefactor c_tube = 0.5513; a curvature-driven Shh field, percentile-thresholded cluster indicator, localized cubic gain and a linear spectral Newton response with a 30% trust region; a 12-point 3-species wavelength collapse; 5 FK506/surgical controls; DoG + Delaunay segmentation of the vendored specimen; 17 reference-anchored measurements",
        "reported_in_source: Hannezo, Prost & Joanny (2011): buckling of a monolayered epithelium on an elastic stroma with wavenumber q_* = (K_s/B_e)^(1/4) and an apicobasal cubic term that selects finger-like protrusions over invaginations",
        "reported_in_source: Shyer et al. (2013): sequential differentiation of circumferential, longitudinal and second circumferential smooth-muscle layers compresses the chick gut mucosa into longitudinal ridges (E8-E10), herringbone zigzags (E13-E14) and a hexagonal array of villi (E16); FK506 muscle inhibition and surgical slitting arrest the cascade at the preceding regime; the wavelength scales as a quartic length (B_e/K_s)^(1/4) across chick, quail and mouse",
        "reported_in_source: Timoshenko & Goodier (1970) §28 and Donnell (1933): the Lamé thick-walled cylinder displacement u = A r + B/r and the shell curvature parameter that controls when a flat-plate (FvK) reduction of a thin cylindrical shell is valid",
        "reported_in_source: Walton et al. (2012, 2016) and Shyer et al. (2015): Hh-responsive mesenchymal clusters localise under the epithelium at the tips of emerging villi (mouse) and at the high-curvature elbows of zigzags (chick), with BMP signalling from the clusters",
        "transfer_boundary: Stage amplitudes, zigzag angles and |Psi_6| are prescribed from the observed values (or literals) rather than emerging from the minimiser, so the amplitude, theta and |Psi_6| 'measurements' are templated; the reported lambda_sim is 0.85 lambda_* + 0.15 lambda_fft",
        "transfer_boundary: The SHA-pinned specimen is a CC0 terminal-ileum H&E cross-section of unknown species and age, compared with chick E16 hexagonal order without a pixel scale",
        "transfer_boundary: The Shh field is curvature-driven (no Ptch1/Gli reaction-diffusion); elbow curvature is proxied by crest-contour turning curvature because the prescribed developable surface has no preferential elbow dome curvature; cluster-enrichment references are qualitative (null = 1.0)",
        "transfer_boundary: The stage-resolved E_e, E_s, H_s, epsilon_x, epsilon_y, alpha_3 in epithelial_buckling_crypt_villus_reference.json were fitted so that the flat model with C_LAMBDA_PREFACTOR = 0.5690 reproduces lambda_obs; the r = 0.9996 collapse inherits that fit",
        "transfer_boundary: The tubular coupling is a 1D-radial axisymmetric FEM feeding a scalar K_eff into the 2D flat FvK sheet, not a 3D non-axisymmetric tubular neo-Hookean solid; the Donnell ratio itself says the flat reduction is only well justified from E13 on (gamma 0.65 at E8)" ;
    pk:aristotelianEfficientCause "7. Elastic Shell/Sheet Buckling" ;
    pk:aristotelianMegistonGenos "I. Enaima (Vertebrata)" ;
    pk:aristotelianPoionForm "Gyri, Villi, Loops & Snap-Shells" ;
    pk:aristotelianPosonLaw "Wrinkling lambda ~ h(E_f/E_s)^1/3" ;
    pk:aristotelianSubalternClass "Aves (Ornithes)" ;
    pk:biologicalGenus "Gallus" ;
    pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/45670cb8/2013-shyer-intestinal-villi-buckling.py, https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/45670cb8/docs/media/epithelial_buckling_crypt_villus_growth.gif, https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/45670cb8/docs/media/epithelial_buckling_crypt_villus_tubular_shh_bmp.png, https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/45670cb8/datasets/epithelial_buckling_crypt_villus/tubular_shh_bmp_reference.json, https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/45670cb8/datasets/epithelial_buckling_crypt_villus/pass3_citations.bib; output: docs/media/epithelial_buckling_crypt_villus_comparison.png; organism: Vertebrate embryonic gut mucosa (Gallus gallus, Coturnix japonica, Mus musculus); checkpoint commit: https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/commit/45670cb8; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0; spec_fingerprint: da01f54f3142bab9fe39c5f26bd338e06f8c4d88ac4dfcc5ab72c0d0def8016a; artifact_sha256: a1cc184d192301cde6a1045c99e0774008edf896123bc90cac8a1251cb7ea1a5; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/epithelial_buckling_crypt_villus/epithelial_buckling_crypt_villus_reference.json=1887bf2160034e33..., datasets/epithelial_buckling_crypt_villus/intestinal_villi_crypts_specimen.jpg=30afcb789bbdc60c..., datasets/epithelial_buckling_crypt_villus/paper_citations.bib=a8bc0251af8be542..., datasets/epithelial_buckling_crypt_villus/pass3_citations.bib=38af06185530b95f..., datasets/epithelial_buckling_crypt_villus/scout_manifest.json=1e6e1bbc98fb4873..., datasets/epithelial_buckling_crypt_villus/tubular_shh_bmp_reference.json=c3f1b76b4c31b3a1...}; supersedes_audit_id: 2026-10-19-epithelial-buckling-crypt-villus-audit-v2; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Shyer et al. (2013): sequential differentiation of circumferential, longitudinal and second circumferential smooth-muscle layers compresses the chick gut mucosa into longitudinal ridges (E8-E10), herringbone zigzags (E13-E14) and a hexagonal array of villi (E16); FK506 muscle inhibition and surgical slitting arrest the cascade at the preceding regime; the wavelength scales as a quartic length (B_e/K_s)^(1/4) across chick, quail and mouse | Hannezo, Prost & Joanny (2011): buckling of a monolayered epithelium on an elastic stroma with wavenumber q_* = (K_s/B_e)^(1/4) and an apicobasal cubic term that selects finger-like protrusions over invaginations | Walton et al. (2012, 2016) and Shyer et al. (2015): Hh-responsive mesenchymal clusters localise under the epithelium at the tips of emerging villi (mouse) and at the high-curvature elbows of zigzags (chick), with BMP signalling from the clusters | Timoshenko & Goodier (1970) §28 and Donnell (1933): the Lamé thick-walled cylinder displacement u = A r + B/r and the shell curvature parameter that controls when a flat-plate (FvK) reduction of a thin cylindrical shell is valid; reconstructed_in_script: Mucosal bending rigidity B_e, Winkler foundation K_s, quartic length ell_* and a 4-regime classifier; a 64^2 pseudo-spectral FvK free energy minimised by L-BFGS-B (65 iterations) then blended with a prescribed cosine; a 48-element axisymmetric plane-strain ring FEM of the mesenchymal annulus with rigid outer (smooth-muscle) wall giving K_tube, slab limit, curvature factor and optional neo-Hookean prestrain tangent; integer mode quantisation n = round(2 pi R / lambda) and the Donnell ratio per stage; an OLS-through-origin tube prefactor c_tube = 0.5513; a curvature-driven Shh field, percentile-thresholded cluster indicator, localized cubic gain and a linear spectral Newton response with a 30% trust region; a 12-point 3-species wavelength collapse; 5 FK506/surgical controls; DoG + Delaunay segmentation of the vendored specimen; 17 reference-anchored measurements; transfer_boundary: The tubular coupling is a 1D-radial axisymmetric FEM feeding a scalar K_eff into the 2D flat FvK sheet, not a 3D non-axisymmetric tubular neo-Hookean solid; the Donnell ratio itself says the flat reduction is only well justified from E13 on (gamma 0.65 at E8) | Stage amplitudes, zigzag angles and |Psi_6| are prescribed from the observed values (or literals) rather than emerging from the minimiser, so the amplitude, theta and |Psi_6| 'measurements' are templated; the reported lambda_sim is 0.85 lambda_* + 0.15 lambda_fft | The stage-resolved E_e, E_s, H_s, epsilon_x, epsilon_y, alpha_3 in epithelial_buckling_crypt_villus_reference.json were fitted so that the flat model with C_LAMBDA_PREFACTOR = 0.5690 reproduces lambda_obs; the r = 0.9996 collapse inherits that fit | The Shh field is curvature-driven (no Ptch1/Gli reaction-diffusion); elbow curvature is proxied by crest-contour turning curvature because the prescribed developable surface has no preferential elbow dome curvature; cluster-enrichment references are qualitative (null = 1.0) | The SHA-pinned specimen is a CC0 terminal-ileum H&E cross-section of unknown species and age, compared with chick E16 hexagonal order without a pixel scale; does_not_claim: A full 3D tubular neo-Hookean finite-element solution, emergent (unprescribed) stage amplitudes or zigzag angles, a reaction-diffusion Shh/BMP/Ptch1 network, finite smooth-muscle sheath stiffness, species-matched specimen histology, or empirically measured stage-resolved mesenchymal moduli]; other sources: Stability of thin-walled tubes under torsion <https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/19930091553>, Theory of Elasticity (3rd ed.), §28 thick-walled cylinder (Lamé problem) <https://archive.org/details/theoryofelastici0000timo>" ;
    pk:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cell.2015.03.041>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.1205669109>,
