<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-shyer-intestinal-villi-buckling-code-traceability> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Hannezo et al. (2011) PRL & Shyer et al. (2013) Science sequential smooth-muscle mucosal buckling into ridges, zigzags, and hexagonal villi — Code-to-model traceability: 89/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "The module header (L1-89) maps every equation to Shyer 2013 Figs. 1-4, Hannezo 2011 Eqs. (5)-(11), Tallinen 2013, Walton 2012/2016, Shyer 2015, Lamé/Timoshenko §28 and Donnell, and names the six Lean theorems; the Pass 3 functions carry docstrings that state the reduction (axisymmetric, rigid wall, curvature-proxy Shh) and the Lean law each implements; the math-KG YAML registers 5 laws with single `file#La-Lb` code loci. Deductions: unsourced literals remain — the 0.92 in the theta fallback (L669), the 155*sqrt(dex+0.8 dey) amplitude fallback (L782), the 0.85/0.15 surface and wavelength blends (L732, L802), mu_eff = 1.25 (dex + 0.85 dey) (L652), the |Psi_6| literals (L811-815) and theta = 58.5 (L677) (-6); the five Pass 3 tunables are described as modelling choices without a cited anchor (-3); the handoff's own admission that the direct Shyer-2015 exp(-d/ell) elbow test gave index < 1 is in a docstring but not surfaced in the figure or measurement notes (-2)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-code-traceability> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/code-traceability" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "2013-shyer-intestinal-villi-buckling.py L652–L652: mu_eff = 1.25 (dex + 0.85 dey): uncited effective-load constants <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/45670cb8/2013-shyer-intestinal-villi-buckling.py#L652-L652>",
        "2013-shyer-intestinal-villi-buckling.py L669–L669: theta fallback atan(sqrt(dey/dex) 0.92): unsourced 0.92 <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/45670cb8/2013-shyer-intestinal-villi-buckling.py#L669-L669>" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-shyer-intestinal-villi-buckling-code-traceability-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-shyer-intestinal-villi-buckling-code-traceability-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-shyer-intestinal-villi-buckling-code-traceability-3> ;
    pk:hasScore 8.9e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-shyer-intestinal-villi-buckling-model-fidelity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Hannezo et al. (2011) PRL & Shyer et al. (2013) Science sequential smooth-muscle mucosal buckling into ridges, zigzags, and hexagonal villi — Model fidelity to source: 88/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "The Hannezo-Shyer quartic length, bending rigidity and Winkler stiffness (L202-237), the 4-regime classifier (L239-254) and the FvK energy are implemented, and Pass 3 adds a genuinely new mechanical layer: a Lamé-verified axisymmetric neo-Hookean ring FEM of the mesenchymal annulus with slab limit, curvature factor and prestrain tangent (L261-365), integer circumferential mode quantisation and the Donnell validity ratio (L368-419), and a curvature-driven Shh/BMP cluster field with a localized cubic gain and linear spectral Newton response (L422-514, L734-793), all with 6 machine-checked Lean theorems. Deductions: the v2 item asked for a 3D tubular FEM and the delivered foundation is 1D-radial axisymmetric feeding a scalar K_eff into a flat sheet, while the script's own Donnell ratio (gamma = 0.65 at E8) says the flat reduction is poorly justified at the ridge stages (-4); the zigzag angle is taken from the observed target with an unsourced 0.92 fallback (L666-669) and the relaxed surface is blended 0.85 prescribed cosine + 0.15 relaxed (L732), so the zigzag geometry is imposed rather than selected (-4); the L-BFGS-B minimiser stops on its 65-iteration limit on an ill-conditioned L_op^2 (L722) and the Pass 3 coupling therefore uses a linearised response rather than re-minimising (-2); the Shh field has no reaction-diffusion kinetics and its elbow curvature is a contour-turning proxy, as the docstring admits (-2); the ring-FEM outer wall is rigid (infinitely stiff smooth muscle) (-1); credit (+1 net) for the ablation flags and the honest statement of every reduction in docstrings." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-model-fidelity> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/model-fidelity" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "2013-shyer-intestinal-villi-buckling.py L666–L677: theta_zz_deg taken from target_theta_zz_deg (observed) with unsourced 0.92 fallback; hexagonal regime theta_zz_deg = 58.5 literal — zigzag geometry is prescribed, not selected <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/45670cb8/2013-shyer-intestinal-villi-buckling.py#L666-L677>",
        "2013-shyer-intestinal-villi-buckling.py L722–L732: L-BFGS-B maxiter 65 on the ill-conditioned L_op^2 followed by the 0.85 prescribed-cosine / 0.15 relaxed blend of the surface <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/45670cb8/2013-shyer-intestinal-villi-buckling.py#L722-L732>" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-shyer-intestinal-villi-buckling-model-fidelity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-shyer-intestinal-villi-buckling-model-fidelity-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-shyer-intestinal-villi-buckling-model-fidelity-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-shyer-intestinal-villi-buckling-model-fidelity-4>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-shyer-intestinal-villi-buckling-model-fidelity-5>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-shyer-intestinal-villi-buckling-model-fidelity-6>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-shyer-intestinal-villi-buckling-model-fidelity-7> ;
    pk:hasScore 8.8e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-shyer-intestinal-villi-buckling-morphometric-validation> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Hannezo et al. (2011) PRL & Shyer et al. (2013) Science sequential smooth-muscle mucosal buckling into ridges, zigzags, and hexagonal villi — Morphometric validation: 84/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "`measure_morphoeval()` (L1632-1832) returns 17 reference-anchored measurements, 8 new in Pass 3: FEM vs Lamé max rel. error 2.1e-5, E16 curvature factor 0.9347, tube lambda RMSE 1.717 um (flat 1.468), mean quantised mode-count error 0.2 ridges, E16 Donnell gamma 0.0698, E14 elbow-localization index 1.4201 (null 1.0), E16 1.1908 clusters per villus, E14 elbow bulge 5.885 um vs 0 ablation; the Pass 2 set (3-species r = 0.9996, alpha = 0.9567, E10 lambda 118.69 vs 118, E16 lambda 80.15 vs 82, specimen Z = 5.5517, CV = 0.2441) is retained with tube-coupled wavelengths. Deductions: the E14 theta = 38.5 vs 38.5 and E16 |Psi_6| = 0.78 vs 0.78 measurements are templated — theta is the observed target (L666-669) and psi6_sim is a literal per regime (L811-815) — and the FK506@E14 |Psi_6| is likewise a formula literal (-6); the reported lambda_sim is 0.85 lambda_* + 0.15 lambda_fft (L802), so the wavelength validation is 85% the analytic prediction rather than the relaxed surface (-3); measurements #1 and #2 are code-vs-closed-form verifications (reference = Lamé, equal by construction) and count as reproducibility evidence, not biological validation (-2); the elbow-bulge magnitude is set by the trust region, as the measurement note itself says (-1); the cluster-enrichment references are null values with no measured enrichment (-1); the stage moduli were fitted to lambda_obs so the flat-model RMSE and the collapse are not independent tests (-3). The honest measurement notes and the ablation-anchored references are credited." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-morphometric-validation> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/morphometric-validation" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "2013-shyer-intestinal-villi-buckling.py L802–L815: lambda_sim = 0.85 lambda_star + 0.15 lambda_fft; psi6_sim = 0.09 / 0.28 + 0.10 (dey/dex) / 0.78 literals per regime — the |Psi_6| and 85% of the wavelength 'measurements' are not measured from the surface <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/45670cb8/2013-shyer-intestinal-villi-buckling.py#L802-L815>" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-shyer-intestinal-villi-buckling-measurement-3-species-mucosal-buckling-wavelength-scaling-correlation-chick-quail-mouse>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-shyer-intestinal-villi-buckling-measurement-axisymmetric-ring-fem-mesenchymal-foundation-stiffness-vs-lam-thick-cylinder-analytic-max-rel-error-6-chick-stages>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-shyer-intestinal-villi-buckling-measurement-chick-5-stage-tubular-ring-fem-fvk-wavelength-rmse-curvature-coupled-lambda-tube-vs-lambda-obs>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-shyer-intestinal-villi-buckling-measurement-chick-e10-1d-parallel-longitudinal-ridge-wavelength-lambda-sim>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-shyer-intestinal-villi-buckling-measurement-chick-e14-2d-herringbone-zigzag-chevron-half-angle-theta-zz-sim>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-shyer-intestinal-villi-buckling-measurement-chick-e14-cluster-induced-elbow-bulge-linear-fvk-response-to-localized-alpha-3-alpha-3-0-60-c-vs-no-signaling-ablation>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-shyer-intestinal-villi-buckling-measurement-chick-e14-shh-bmp-mesenchymal-cluster-elbow-localization-index-cluster-mass-at-zigzag-elbows-uniform-expectation>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-shyer-intestinal-villi-buckling-measurement-chick-e16-donnell-shell-curvature-ratio-gamma-e-e-h-e-r-2-k-eff-flat-plate-fvk-validity>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-shyer-intestinal-villi-buckling-measurement-chick-e16-hexagonal-villi-bond-orientational-order-psi-6>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-shyer-intestinal-villi-buckling-measurement-chick-e16-hexagonal-villi-spacing-lambda-sim>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-shyer-intestinal-villi-buckling-measurement-chick-e16-shh-bmp-mesenchymal-clusters-per-villus-n-clusters-expected-villi-in-the-4x4-period-hexagonal-box>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-shyer-intestinal-villi-buckling-measurement-chick-e16-tubular-curvature-factor-k-tube-k-slab-of-the-mesenchymal-annulus-h-s-r-lumen-0-248>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-shyer-intestinal-villi-buckling-measurement-chick-e8-e16-integer-circumferential-mode-count-on-the-tube-mean-n-quantized-n-ridges-obs>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-shyer-intestinal-villi-buckling-measurement-cross-species-log-log-quartic-length-scale-exponent-alpha-lambda-ell-alpha>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-shyer-intestinal-villi-buckling-measurement-fk506-e6-circular-smooth-muscle-ablation-negative-control-amplitude>,
